A frontend module declares its schema by exporting a `configSchema` object from `src/config-schema.ts` and registering it with `defineConfigSchema(moduleName, configSchema)`, usually at startup in `src/index.ts`. Each setting is an object with `_type`, `_default`, and optionally `_description`. Implementers then override those values in their configuration files, keyed by module name.

**Documentation**

- The main guide is "The Configuration System" (RFC-14). It says every module should provide defaults, since all configuration is optional in O3 3.0. It also shows the `_type`, `_default`, and `_description` keywords, and warns against raw values in place of schema objects and against naming elements with `_` or the reserved keys `Display conditions` and `Translation overrides`. @file:{openmrs-contrib-o3-docs::content/en-US/docs/configuration-system.mdx:17-66}
- The type list (`Type.String`, `Type.Number`, `Type.Boolean`, and so on) is in the same guide. @file:{openmrs-contrib-o3-docs::content/en-US/docs/configuration-system.mdx:102-110}
- The "Configuring individual frontend modules" section of the Configure O3 guide gives the concrete `src/config-schema.ts` pattern, using the Programs module as its example, and shows a matching TypeScript interface. @file:{openmrs-contrib-o3-docs::content/en-US/docs/configure-o3/overview.mdx:156-179}

**Implementation**

- `defineConfigSchema` validates the schema, merges it with the implicit schema (which adds the reserved keys), and stores it under the module name in the config store. @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-config/src/module-config/module-config.ts:357-378}
- A typical call site is the login app's entry point, which imports its `configSchema` and calls `defineConfigSchema(moduleName, configSchema)`. @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/apps/esm-login-app/src/index.ts:20-20}
- The primary navigation app follows the same pattern, with its schema in `config-schema.ts`. @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/apps/esm-primary-navigation-app/src/config-schema.ts:3-3}

**Gaps**

- I did not read the code that merges an implementer's config file over the defaults, so the override mechanism is documented but not traced end to end.
- I did not read the `_type` validation logic in `validateConfigSchema`.

